SUDO(1)                        User Commands                         SUDO(1)

NAME
    sudo - authenticate again and run the armed image as the administrator

SYNOPSIS
    sudo

DESCRIPTION
    Ask for your password, and if it is right, start the image the loader
    has armed with administrator identity. With nothing armed it says so
    after authenticating.

    sudo takes no argument. A password on the command line would be echoed
    to the console and the serial log, so it is read at a masked prompt
    (by the console server, or the kernel's own reader without one), never
    echoed, and wiped from the shell's memory once the kernel has checked
    it.

SECURITY
    Wrong passwords count towards the account's lockout, which the kernel
    enforces and no file can change.

SEE ALSO
    passwd(1), spawn(1), login.conf(5)
